orce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Is this really the best place to fix the issue?\r\nWhile making `Callable` / `Signal` comparisons predictable across sessions is very defensible, the 'real' issue in my mind is that `.tscn` files depend on the intrinsic comparison order of these objects in the first place. \r\nAs a file type, I'm wondering whether they shouldn't be defining their own comparison order, one that's focused on readability and well-defined stability rather than speed. The change presented here makes comparisons _very slightly_ slower, establishing a precedent of sacrificing core comparison speed for the sake of predictability, which I'm not quite sure is the way to go long-term.\r\n\r\nEdit: Will discuss in the core meeting.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119574#pullrequestreview-4320062151","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119574","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119574#pullrequestreview-4320062151"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119574"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-19T14:46:17Z","commit_id":"b3512e17b4e37a480e22222a23d032e34bbdd3c0"}]